#{[17592186184235 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186184857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184235 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186184864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184235 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying Several Transformations: Horizontal Shift Followed By Horizontal Stretch Inside Parentheses" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184235 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186183917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184235 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b2252e35-f1c6-5d83-853a-9090c253fd35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186184965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186185019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186185020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186185031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186185032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1045 "Constructing Functions Using Transformations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186185019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184429 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f4c9f3cd-60b1-585d-8adf-32b7b25fe2df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184965 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186185031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184965 #edb/ref 1061 28410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184965 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "24f23941-c700-549c-9117-5700b1664f45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184965 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185019 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186184965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185019 #edb/ref 1061 37620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185019 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f7f231fe-9e17-5908-8d88-384170536e99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185019 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186185348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185020 #edb/ref 1061 37621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185020 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "16c93c37-5e32-5491-a3b7-a262662bf8fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185020 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185031 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186185032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185031 #edb/ref 1061 37731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185031 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "457bac5a-22a8-5ad9-9412-de0bf90d6a87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185031 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185032 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186185020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185032 #edb/ref 1061 37732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185032 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "69065bb9-317b-55a5-84c9-5770500328b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185032 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185348 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we have the graph of a function $y=f(x)$ to which we apply the following transformations in the order listed:\n\n1. translation by $\\color{blue}5$ units up\n2. translation by $\\color{red}4$ units left\n3. stretch by a scale factor of $\\color{purple}3$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\nWhat is the final function expression after applying all the transformations?\n\nTo find the final expression, we apply each transformation in turn.\n\n1. Translating the graph of $y=f(x)$ up by $\\color{blue}5$ units is equivalent to adding $\\color{blue}5$ to the function expression. Applying this transformation, we obtain $y=f(x)+{\\color{blue}5}$.\n2. Translating the graph of $y=f(x)+5$ by $\\color{red}4$ units to the left is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $(x+{\\color{red}{4}})$. Applying this transformation, we obtain $y =f(x+{\\color{red}4})+{\\color{blue}5}$.\n3. Stretching the graph of $y=f(x+4)+5$ by a scale factor of $\\color{purple}3$ parallel to the $y$-axis is equivalent to multiplying the function expression by $3$. Applying this transformation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= 3 \\cdot (f(x + 4) + 5) \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot f(x + 4) + 3 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&= 3f(x + 4) + 15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final function expression is\n\n$$\ny=3f(x+4)+15\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185348 #edb/ref 1065 6206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185348 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6e9cbac2-104e-55b2-a0ca-d481f24c1cc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185348 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192749 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192749 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192749 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192749 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192749 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192749 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing the Sine of an Angle in Terms of a Reference Angle in Radians" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192749 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192749 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "961a5c28-9e1e-5b0c-bd04-63068bebd8b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192750 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing the Cosine of an Angle in Terms of a Reference Angle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192750 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192750 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5a7d5897-3360-59fb-9f64-2f9f641290be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192751 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing the Tangent of an Angle in Terms of a Reference Angle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192751 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192751 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4e677d9